# Seed ksud, and run the KSU autoinstall script once boot completes.
#
# Seeding ksud: on a wiped device /data/adb/ksud does not exist until the
# manager app is opened, and without it KernelSU is completely inert:
#   init: Command 'exec u:r:ksu:s0 root -- /data/adb/ksud post-fs-data'
#         failed: Cannot find '/data/adb/ksud'
# ...and the same for `services` and `boot-completed`. `copy` is a built-in init
# command, so this needs no exec and no new sepolicy. It is the same binary the
# manager would copy, shipped in this ROM, so it matches this kernel. Rewritten
# every boot, which also repairs a deleted or truncated ksud.
#
# KSU's own post-fs-data exec (init.rc) runs before this action, so on the very
# first boot after a wipe that stage is still skipped -- harmless, as there are
# no modules to mount yet. `services` and `boot-completed` come later and do
# find it.
on post-fs-data
    mkdir /data/adb 0700 root root
    copy /product/app/KernelSUNext/lib/arm64/libksud.so /data/adb/ksud
    chmod 0755 /data/adb/ksud
    chown root root /data/adb/ksud

# Run the script as an init service rather than through one of KernelSU's script
# directories. This ksud runs NEITHER /data/adb/service.d (its two mentions are
# only variables in the util_functions.sh snippet it hands to module installers)
# NOR boot-completed.d; a boot-completed.d that works on a configured device is
# being run by one of the installed modules. post-fs-data.d it does run, but
# init copies into /data too late for that stage on a wiped device -- exactly
# the boot this exists for.
#
# `seclabel u:r:su:s0` is what makes init able to exec a shell script at all:
# without it, init refuses with "has incorrect label or no domain transition
# from u:r:init:s0". This is the same pattern init.debuglog.rc already uses on
# this device. PRODUCT_COPY_FILES into bin/ installs it 0755, so no exec bit
# handling is needed.
service ksu_autoinstall /system_ext/bin/ksu-autoinstall.sh
    user root
    group root
    seclabel u:r:su:s0
    disabled
    oneshot

on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    start ksu_autoinstall
